00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:03.399
Here are some examples of the local phrase
searches, again pointing to the directory

00:11:03.399 --> 00:11:04.709
on Rose, the postings directory.

00:11:04.709 --> 00:11:05.709
local-phrase-search -path /Volumes/rose/Postings
-count "catabolite repressor*"

00:11:05.709 --> 00:11:06.709
local-phrase-search -path /Volumes/rose/Postings
-query "catabolite repressor*" | fetch-pubmed

00:11:06.709 --> 00:11:12.019
It can count them or get them, the IDs, for
you, and pass them to fetch-pubmed.

00:11:12.019 --> 00:11:16.600
You can also set an environmtnt variable that
will make it so you don't have to include

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.999
